    "result_text": "The full test suite passes \u2014 **26 tests, 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the `customerCode` format from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\n- **`generateCustomerCode`** now takes the owner's city as well as their last name. It builds `CITY3` from the upper-cased first three letters of the city, keeps `LAST3` from the last name, and computes `NNNN` as a **per-city** sequence \u2014 one more than the number of existing owners in that city (cities matched case-insensitively so owners sharing a `CITY3` prefix share a sequence) \u2014 instead of the old global owner count.\n- **Call site** (`addOwner`) updated to pass `owner.getCity()`.\n\nEverything derived from the customer code rebuilds automatically: the `membershipNumber` is defined in `OwnerMapper` as `customerCode + \"-M\" + <YY>`, so it now carries the new city-prefixed code with no further change. The `Cp14` test confirms this (it recomputes the expected value from the returned `customerCode`, format-agnostic), `Cp09` confirms the `SYD-ALP-`/`SYD-BRA-` prefixes and consecutive per-city sequence, and `Cp16` confirms the `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}` shape.",
